// Diagnosing a wrong finding (docs/architecture/learning-loop.md LL4, LL11).
//
// A judge's finding was marked wrong, by a person or by a line run's proof.
// The line that leads the finding's project starts this graph for it
// (convex/judgeReview.ts), with the finding (sg-N) as the goal. One short
// session answers one question, whether the fact a correct judgment needed
// was missing from what the judge saw or there and misread, and the record
// step files the finding as a case against the part of the judge at fault:
// its prompt, the input the product builds for it, or the extractor that
// froze the moment. Cases against one part gather into one problem, which
// runs on the project's line like any change.
digraph judge_review {
  graph [goal="A wrong finding", stack="Judge review · $run_date"]
  rankdir=LR

  start [shape=Mdiamond, label="Start"]
  exit  [shape=Msquare,  label="Exit"]

  diagnose [label="Diagnose", backend=session, agent=claude, timeout=1800, prompt="@line/diagnose.md"]

  record [label="File the case", shape=parallelogram, timeout=300,
    script="cast signal diagnosis $goal --result $diagnose.json"]

  start -> diagnose
  diagnose -> record
  record -> exit
}
